# Visual Editor — the source

This folder is `~/Sites/statamic-addon-visual-editor-vue`. It is the source: all Visual Editor code is written here, and Packagist builds the package the site runs from it. **Never edit** `~/Sites/statamic-addon-visual-editor` (the old restore point) or any `… copy` / `…-app` / `…-vue-backup-*` folder.

## Surfaces

- Kernel (not Vue), under `resources/js/`: `bridge.js` + `bridge/`, `preview.js`, `mirror.js`, `overlay-host.js`, `cp.js` + `cp-shell/`, `code-dock.js` + `dock/`, `lib/protocol.js` (the site's `docs/kvalitetsrunde-brief.md` §4.2)
- A CP panel: one Vue app under `resources/js/cp/surfaces/`. No import of the kernel or `cp.js`.
- Fieldtypes: own Vue files via `Statamic.component()`. Do not wrap Statamic's `replicator`, `icon`, `bard`, `grid`.

One task = one surface. After a change: `npm run isolate`.

Never write the site's `public/vendor`. Never rebuild overlay-host, preview or bridge alone. `resources/dist/build` is the editor — if a hashed file addon.js imports is gone, the toolbar is gone.
